<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44392" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">singultĭo</span></b> , īre,
			v. n.
		singultus. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>To hiccup</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aut bilem vomunt aut singultiunt,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cels. 5, 26, 19</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Plin. 23, 1, 24, § 48</span></i>; <i>to sob</i>, <i><span class="en">App. M. 3, p.
				133, 40</span></i>.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, of a hen, <i>to
			cluck</i>, <i><span class="en">Col. 8, 11, 15</span></i>.—*
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>to throb</i> with
			pleasure: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vena,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Pers.
					6, 72</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
